            <ArticleTitle>[A boy with a white striped knee on a radiograph].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>D1575</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 10-year-old boy presented at the radiology department with pain in the right knee. Radiographs of the knee revealed dens metaphyseal bands and subchondral epiphyseal sclerosis as a result of periodic bisphosphonate administration for the treatment of Legg-Calvé-Perthes disease three years ago.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
